# Documentation lock manifest.
#
# One rule per line, `tier: glob`. The LAST matching rule wins, so promoting a
# file is a line appended at the end and this file is its own history of
# promotions. A path that matches no rule is `free`.
#
#   hard-locked  may not change at all; `make unlock PATH=... REASON="..."` is
#                the only way through, and it leaves a record in UNLOCKS.md
#   append-only  existing lines may never be removed or modified; additions are
#                allowed anywhere in the file, including under an existing entry
#   free         mutable by design; listed explicitly so that mutability reads as
#                a decision rather than an oversight
#
# Enforced by scripts/lock-guard.py over the diff, from .githooks/pre-commit
# locally and from the pre-receive hook on the remote. `make install-hooks`
# activates the local ones; `make check-locks` runs the same check by hand.
# Tiers are promoted as the pack matures; each promotion is a committed change,
# and this file is hard-locked, so each is a `make unlock PATH=.doc-locks` with
# its reason in UNLOCKS.md. Tiers never go down: the guard compares the manifest
# before and after a change and refuses any path whose tier would be lowered,
# whichever glob does it (demotion rule). The change that judges a commit is
# always read from HEAD (or, on the remote, from the revision being replaced),
# never from the working tree, so a commit cannot relax a lock for itself.

version: 1

# --- free: the living documents. Changing is what they are for. ---------------
# PLAN.md drops completed items, GAPS.md retires closed rows, TRACEABILITY.md
# rewrites a status when evidence arrives. A lock here would be a lie.
free: PLAN.md
free: GAPS.md
free: TRACEABILITY.md
free: AGENTS.md
free: CLAUDE.md
free: README.md
free: Makefile
free: scripts/**
free: .githooks/**


# specs/ stays free until the baseline is stamped: review rounds still rewrite
# statements and their provenance tags. The freeze promotes it to hard-locked.
free: specs/**

# --- append-only: the record of what happened ---------------------------------
# The event log is the source of truth for the streams that use it. Removing a
# line is caught here; changing one is caught by the hash chain, which is what
# `make verify-chain` and the `chain-intact` rule of check-docs walk.
append-only: .log/events.jsonl
append-only: UNLOCKS.md

# DECISIONS.md and QUESTIONS.md are free because they are generated, not
# authored: each is the projection of a stream of the log. Free does not mean
# unguarded. The `projection-fresh` rule of check-docs rebuilds both and compares
# byte for byte, so a hand edit fails the gate rather than becoming the record,
# and the rebuild scripts have to be able to write the files, which a lock would
# prevent. A card that moves between Blocking, Open and Resolved moves because an
# event says so, not because someone edited a section.
free: DECISIONS.md
free: QUESTIONS.md

# The lock layer guards itself. The guard, the ceremony script, the hooks and
# this manifest are hard-locked from the first commit: a guard that the diff it
# judges may rewrite is no guard. Updating any of them is a ceremony.
hard-locked: scripts/lock-guard.py
hard-locked: scripts/unlock.sh
hard-locked: .githooks/**
hard-locked: .doc-locks

# --- hard-locked: the raw material -------------------------------------------
# What the owner actually said. Nothing in the pack ever edits it; a new or
# corrected input is a deliberate, recorded act.
hard-locked: docs/inputs/**

# --- promoted at the freeze (appended by the freeze, not written here) --------
#   hard-locked: specs/**

# Frozen at the baseline, 2026-09-23: the contract itself.
hard-locked: specs/**
